WP07 security and no-claim proof

Negative cases covered by tests:
- Store package rows keep runtimeState=notClaimed.
- Store package rows keep foregroundState=notClaimed.
- Store package rows keep runningDurationMs=0.
- Store package rows keep foregroundDurationMs=0.
- Runtime process merge requires packageId or AppUserModelId.
- Display label and executable path refs alone do not merge Store package rows.

Explicitly not claimed:
- live Store/UWP/AppX/MSIX enumeration;
- Store API access;
- install approval;
- purchase approval;
- journal replay stability;
- service read model;
- portal UI safety for package metadata;
- package-wide blocking or enforcement.
